  "geometry_notes": "One column only is shown at a time (the slider replaces the four side-by-side panels). Planes: 7 squares, each 2.0 x 2.0 world units lying in the XZ plane (+X screen-right, +Z receding diagonal), centered on the Y axis, stacked at y = 0, 1.6, 3.2, 4.8, 6.4, 8.0, 9.6 (total stack height 9.6, roughly 5x its width, matching the tall thin columns in the source). Plane order bottom→top: input, after linear1, after relu1, after linear2, after relu2, after linear3, after softmax; the six labeled transitions in the legend sit between consecutive planes. Each plane has a dark-gray border (#444444, ~1.5px) and a faint 4x4 internal grid (#cccccc). Gray dashed corner-to-corner scaffolding lines (#999999, dash 0.06) connect matching corners of adjacent planes. ~70 datapoints, ~35 red and ~35 blue, sphere/point radius ~0.035 world units. Red #ee1111, blue #1111ee, both drawn with ~0.7 opacity; trajectory curves are dashed, same hue as their point, thin (~1px), dash length ~0.05. Layout of the data by height and training progress t in [0,1]: bottom plane always a dense isotropic cluster of radius ~0.35 centered at the plane origin with red and blue fully interleaved (identical at all t). Moving upward, red points contract toward the column axis — lateral spread shrinking from 0.35 at the bottom to ~0.08 at the top when t=1, only to ~0.25 when t=0 — forming the tight vertical red bundle. Blue points migrate monotonically in +X (screen-right) as height increases; peak lateral offset of the blue cloud at the upper planes is ~0.3 units at t=0, ~0.9 at t=0.33, ~1.6 at t=0.66, and ~2.6 at t=1, so at late training the blue trajectories overshoot the plane edge and fan out to the right of the stack (exactly as in the rightmost source column). Relu planes additionally clamp roughly a third of the points onto the plane's axis lines (a visible line/corner concentration). On the top softmax plane red collapses to a small cluster at the left/center and blue to a cluster at the right corner. Legend column drawn to the left of the stack at x ~ -3.2, spanning the same y range: six rounded-rectangle labels (white fill, dark gray 1px stroke, monospace text) reading bottom→top linear, relu, linear, relu, linear, softmax, each preceded by a short upward arrow, vertically aligned with the gap between the corresponding pair of planes. Beneath everything at y ~ -1.2 a horizontal arrow spanning the figure width labeled 'Training iteration' (serif text) with four tick marks and two sets of ellipsis dots between them; the slider handle rides along this axis.",
